From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sebastien Marie <semarie@kapouay.eu.org>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 09:43:01 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] CA 153718: use OPENSSL_ENABLE_MD5_VERIFY=1 in OpenvSwitch

Original patch at https://github.com/xcp-ng-rpms/openvswitch/blob/dbed68cb6d068bb6beef20d68aecece029d74684/SOURCES/CA-153718-md5-verification-dvsc.patch

The original patch was adding `export OPENSSL_ENABLE_MD5_VERIFY=1` in
`ovs-start` script.

`OPENSSL_ENABLE_MD5_VERIFY` was never an upstream OpenSSL feature. It came from
a Fedora/RHEL downstream patch that disabled MD5 for certificate signature
verification and used this variable as an opt-out. In 2014 the Fedora OpenSSL
maintainer [suggested setting it in the OpenVPN client and
server](https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=1157260) to allow
verification of MD5-signed certificates, while saying he would not recommend
doing so.

The changelog documents it as:

> disable verification of certificate, CRL, and OCSP signatures using MD5 if OPENSSL_ENABLE_MD5_VERIFY environment variable is not set.

Setting it in `ovs-start` script means ovs is expected to accept MD5
certificates, CRL or OCSP signatures (depending the current security level),
like with an unpatched OpenSSL.

As OpenSSL rpm still has [the disable MD5
patch](https://github.com/xcp-ng-rpms/openssl/blob/5ddabd58ecadf0c96408edd1309a4465da426518/SOURCES/0006-Disable-signature-verification-with-totally-unsafe-h.patch),
we might still want the change in OVS in order to relax the restriction and
makes OpenSSL to work as unpatched one.

Move the export in ovs-lib (sourced by openvswitch daemons) as the xenserver is gone.

Signed-off-by: Sebastien Rodot <sebastien.rodot@vates.tech>
---
 utilities/ovs-lib.in | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/utilities/ovs-lib.in b/utilities/ovs-lib.in
index dded0b7c7..b27da364f 100644
--- a/utilities/ovs-lib.in
+++ b/utilities/ovs-lib.in
@@ -30,6 +30,12 @@ datadir=${OVS_PKGDATADIR-'@pkgdatadir@'}        # /usr/share/openvswitch
 bindir=${OVS_BINDIR-'@bindir@'}                 # /usr/bin
 sbindir=${OVS_SBINDIR-'@sbindir@'}              # /usr/sbin
 
+# Set OPENSSL_ENABLE_MD5_VERIFY=1 to ovs to accept MD5 certificates, CRL or OCSP 
+# signatures (depending the current security level), like with an unpatched 
+# OpenSSL.
+OPENSSL_ENABLE_MD5_VERIFY=1
+export OPENSSL_ENABLE_MD5_VERIFY
+
 # /etc/openvswitch or /var/lib/openvswitch
 if test X"$OVS_DBDIR" != X; then
     dbdir=$OVS_DBDIR
